# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ns}
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3}
{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{t: I HOPE THAT I DON’T FALL IN LOVE WITH YOU (In G) – Hootie & Blowfish}
{st: (Waits) }
{artist: Hootie and the Blowfish}
{composer: Tom Waits}


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xrf9Dkk96Ng  (Capo 5)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and (CaddG) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  This is a lovely song to fingerpick but is easier to do so in the key G rather than the key of C (at least for me it is).  You can still chord strum this version if you wish.

TIP:  Instead of chords to begin each verse, try picking the individual notes and begin strumming with the third word (G).  (f#) is 4th string/4th fret, (g) is open 3rd string, (a) is 3rd string/2nd fret.  (Notes may or may not transpose).


